@@ -3,3 +3,18 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer, PointerError } from "json-toolkit";
+
+resolvePointer({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, "/foo/1"); // "baz"
+resolvePointer(doc, ""); // the whole document
+```
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the value the pointer refers to (`null` is a valid result). It throws a
+`PointerError` whose `code` is `"INVALID_POINTER"` (bad syntax or escape, e.g. `foo`, `/a~2`) or `"UNRESOLVABLE"`
+(missing member, out-of-range or non-canonical array index such as `01`, `-`, or traversing a non-container).
+Only own properties resolve, so `/__proto__` and `/constructor` on ordinary objects fail. The document is never
+mutated. The URI fragment form (RFC 6901 §6) is not supported.
